course: dictionary
lesson: 4420
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A hamlet is a very small village, often with no church. Hamlets are the smallest places where people live together: hamlet, then village, then town, then city, from smallest to largest.
explain: A capital letter can change the meaning. Hamlet with a capital H is a name, the title of a famous play by William Shakespeare, and of its main character, a prince of Denmark. Shakespeare's plays use names like Hamlet, so check for a capital letter first.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is right. In «The class read Hamlet and then acted out the scenes», the word scenes and the word read point to a play, not a village. Always ask what would make sense in the sentence.
fact: A hamlet is a very small village, often with no church.
fact: The order from smallest to largest is hamlet, village, town, city.
fact: «Hamlet» with a capital letter is the name of a play by William Shakespeare.
fact: Shakespeare wrote «Hamlet» around 1600 for the Globe theatre in London.
fact: «Shuffled off this mortal coil» means died. It comes from Shakespeare's Hamlet and is used jokingly.
exercise: What is a hamlet? | A big farm with many animals | A famous play by Shakespeare | A very large city with tall buildings | *A very small village, often with no church
exercise: Which is the largest place? | *A city | A village | A hamlet | A town
exercise: «Hamlet» with a capital H, as in the title of a book, is what? | A kind of bread | *A famous play by William Shakespeare | A town hall | A small village
test: Which list goes from smallest to largest? | *hamlet, village, town, city | city, town, village, hamlet | village, hamlet, city, town
test: «Shuffled off this mortal coil» is a joking way to say what? | Got lost | Went on holiday | *Died | Won a prize
exam: In «The class read Hamlet and then acted out the scenes», what is Hamlet? | A tiny village with no church | *A famous play by Shakespeare | A small town by the sea | A kind of hat
